q("he-101", I, 1, HE, "A flask full of coloured water is placed in a bath of hot water. The liquid rises in the thin tube as shown. Why?", "The water in the flask expands", [W("The water in the flask contracts", "reversed", "A liquid contracts when it loses heat."), W("The water in the flask becomes heavier", "wrong-idea", "Heating does not add mass."), W("Air from the bath enters the flask", "wrong-idea", "The flask is closed. The liquid itself changes.")], ["The water gains heat, expands and has to rise up the tube."], lambda: flask_tube(0.72, 0.42, "hot water", "Flask in a bath"))
q("he-102", I, 1, HE, "The same flask is moved to a bath of ice water. The liquid goes down the tube as shown. What does this show?", "A liquid contracts when it loses heat", [W("A liquid expands when it loses heat", "reversed", "The level went down, so the liquid took up less space."), W("A liquid expands when it gains heat", "wrong-idea", "The liquid was cooled, not heated, in this test."), W("A liquid does not change when it loses heat", "wrong-idea", "The level changed, so the liquid changed.")], ["The level fell because the cooled liquid contracted."], lambda: flask_tube(0.2, 0.42, "ice water", "Flask in a bath"))
q("he-103", I, 1, HE, "A balloon is stretched over the neck of a flask. The flask is placed in hot water and the balloon becomes bigger as shown. Why?", "The air in the flask gains heat and expands", [W("Hot water enters the flask and pushes up the balloon", "wrong-idea", "The water stays outside the flask."), W("The air in the flask gains mass", "wrong-idea", "No air is added, so the mass stays the same."), W("The air in the flask contracts", "reversed", "Air contracts only when it loses heat.")], ["The warmed air expands and fills the balloon."], lambda: balloon(44, "hot water", "Flask and balloon"))
q("he-104", I, 1, HE, "A flask with a balloon on its neck is placed in ice water. The balloon becomes smaller as shown. Why?", "The air in the flask loses heat and contracts", [W("The air in the flask gains heat and expands", "reversed", "The ice water takes heat away from the air."), W("The ice water enters the balloon", "wrong-idea", "The water stays outside the flask."), W("The air in the flask turns into a liquid", "wrong-idea", "Air does not turn into a liquid in ice water.")], ["Cooled air contracts, so the balloon shrinks."], lambda: balloon(13, "ice water", "Flask and balloon"))
q("he-105", I, 1, HE, "A metal ball can only just pass through a metal ring when both are at room temperature. Which of the following will stop the ball from passing through?", "Heating the ball only", [W("Heating the ring only", "reversed", "The ring expands, so its hole is bigger."), W("Cooling the ball only", "reversed", "The ball contracts and is smaller."), W("Leaving both in the room for a while", "wrong-idea", "Nothing changes, so the ball still passes.")], ["Only a bigger ball will not fit. Heating the ball makes it expand."], None)
