q("he-201", C, 2, RD, "Three rods P, Q and R of the same size are heated at one end. The graph shows the temperature at the other end. Which statement is correct?", "Heat travels through R faster than through P", [W("Heat travels through P faster than through R", "reversed", "R's temperature rose faster."), W("Heat travels through Q and R at the same speed", "wrong-reading", "The lines for Q and R are different."), W("Heat does not travel through P", "wrong-reading", "P's temperature also rose, but slowly.")], ["R's far end got hot sooner, so R is the better conductor."], lambda: graph(["0", "2", "4", "6", "8"], [("P", [20, 24, 28, 32, 36]), ("Q", [20, 30, 40, 48, 55]), ("R", [20, 42, 60, 74, 84])], 100, "Time (min)", "Temperature (" + D + ")", "Temperature at the far end", ystep=20, W=360, H=250, legend="br"))
